  "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z\\ge -2.15).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/f814b532742940206d119c1aa30746b128ab6ede249128e55fc949a1051220c9.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=\u03a6(z).\n$$\n\nSince the total area under the graph equals $1,$ we can express the required probability in terms of $\u03a6(z)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -2.15) & =1-P(Z<-2.15) \\\\  & =1-\u03a6(-2.15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/9e2cf363bd0732c4669c4653d83f505826af605f2bc719a4f39135d233456b57.png)\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\n\u03a6(-2.15)=0.0158.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -2.15) & =1-\u03a6(-2.15) \\\\  & =1-0.0158 \\\\  & =0.9842.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
